{"causes": ["The 1204 Fourth Crusade's sack of Constantinople and the subsequent Latin occupation created a fractured political landscape the Palaiologan Empire sought to reunite.", "Emperor Michael VIII Palaiologos's reconquest of Constantinople in 1261 necessitated a strong military and loyal aristocracy to consolidate and expand the restored empire.", "The prominent aristocratic lineage of the Komnenos, Doukas, Angelos, and Petraliphas families provided John Raoul Petraliphas with inherent status and military opportunities within the Byzantine state."], "effects": ["John Raoul Petraliphas's military leadership contributed to the stabilization of the Byzantine Empire's western frontiers against Latin and Greek rivals.", "His high administrative and military appointments strengthened Emperor Michael VIII Palaiologos's control during the critical early years of his reign.", "The continued prominence of the Raoul-Petraliphas family in subsequent generations demonstrated the enduring aristocratic influence he represented in Byzantine politics."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "michael-viii-palaiologos", "sourceName": "Michael VIII Palaiologos", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "john-raoul-petraliphas", "targetName": "John Raoul Petraliphas", "context": "John Raoul Petraliphas served as a trusted military commander and administrator under Emperor Michael VIII Palaiologos from the 1260s until 1274."}, {"sourceSlug": "john-raoul-petraliphas", "sourceName": "John Raoul Petraliphas", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "palaiologan-restoration", "targetName": "Palaiologan Restoration", "context": "Petraliphas was a key military figure in the Palaiologan Byzantine Empire's efforts to reassert control over former territories after the reconquest of Constantinople in 1261."}, {"sourceSlug": "john-raoul-petraliphas", "sourceName": "John Raoul Petraliphas", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "byzantine-empire", "targetName": "Byzantine Empire", "context": "John Raoul Petraliphas's entire military and administrative career unfolded within the political and geographical bounds of the Byzantine Empire during its Palaiologan period."}, {"sourceSlug": "constantinople", "sourceName": "Constantinople", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "john-raoul-petraliphas", "targetName": "John Raoul Petraliphas", "context": "The reconquest of Constantinople in 1261 by Michael VIII Palaiologos provided the impetus and context for John Raoul Petraliphas's rise as a key military commander."}, {"sourceSlug": "john-raoul-petraliphas", "sourceName": "John Raoul Petraliphas", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "byzantine-aristocracy", "targetName": "Byzantine Aristocracy", "context": "As a member of several powerful dynastic families, Petraliphas exemplified and reinforced the influence of the Byzantine aristocracy in imperial governance and military affairs."}], "places": [{"name": "Constantinople, Byzantine Empire", "role": "Imperial Capital"}, {"name": "Macedonia, Byzantine Empire", "role": "Military Command Region"}, {"name": "Thessaly, Byzantine Empire", "role": "Campaign Area"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: John Raoul Petraliphas", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "john-raoul-petraliphas"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q498444", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Raoul_Petraliphas"], "tags": ["Military Leaders & Commanders", "conflict-and-resolution", "geopolitical-linkage", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "John Raoul Petraliphas was a significant regional figure whose military commands and administrative roles helped consolidate Michael VIII Palaiologos's authority and stabilize the Byzantine Empire's frontiers during a critical post-reconquest period, contributing to the dynasty's early successes.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-08-08T06:34:34Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#31243644909", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "John Komnenos Raoul Doukas Angelos Petraliphas was a Byzantine noble and military commander during the reign of Emperor Michael VIII Palaiologos.", "newValue": "John Komnenos Raoul Doukas Angelos Petraliphas, a scion of the most prominent Byzantine aristocratic families, emerged as a vital military commander and high-ranking official during the nascent years of the restored Palaiologan Empire. Active from the 1260s until his death in 1274, he was instrumental in consolidating Emperor Michael VIII Palaiologos's authority following the Byzantine reconquest of Constantinople in 1261, serving as a pillar of the new regime's military and administrative structure. His career reflects the intricate interplay of dynastic power and military prowess essential for the empire's survival after decades of Latin rule.

Elevated to the prestigious ranks of *protosebastos* and *strategos autokrator* (commander-in-chief), Petraliphas was entrusted with critical military commands in the Balkans. He led campaigns aimed at reasserting Byzantine control over fragmented territories, particularly against Latin remnants and rival Greek states in Epirus and Thessaly. His military efforts contributed significantly to the stabilization of Michael VIII's rule, securing the empire's western frontiers against external threats and internal dissent during a period of intense geopolitical flux in the Aegean and Balkan regions.

